Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 16:39:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03493/11362] [outer-loop] Q-head step 4 BREAKTHROUGH: tuned
 spatial value routes ls20-L1 7.6x faster than blind

The strong spatial value (discrimination 36: on-path 11 vs far 48) DOES route -- it was just
under-weighted. heuristic_weight sweep (depth + w*value), ls20-L1, vs blind's 1777 expansions:
  w=0.05->1.25x  w=0.1->1.34x  w=0.3->1.81x  w=1.0->3.12x  w=3.0->6.81x  w=10->7.63x (233 exp!)

The verifier-as-Q-head WORKS strongly: a learned dense value gives exactly the per-step gradient
every hand/LLM goal lacked, routing 7.6x more efficiently once (1) the architecture preserves
spatial position and (2) the A* weight trusts the reliable value. Monotonic in weight -> the value
is reliable enough to follow nearly greedily.

CALIBRATION: this is a per-game EFFICIENCY win on a level blind ALREADY solves (L1), trained on
ls20's own blind trace. The CRUCIAL untested prize: does the value-Q-head reach levels blind CANNOT
(deepening to L2+, or hard games)? That is the next test.

verdict: success: spatial_value_weight_tuned_strong_routing_speedup (7.63x)

